WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.901
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.567
You're here. Thank you.
You made it.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:07.067
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:08.567
Fun show tonight.

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:10.200
Cameron Diaz
on the show tonight.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.067
That's our pal.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:13.467
-Cammy D.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.434
-Let's get to some news, guys.

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:16.901
Well, it finally happened.

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:19.200
After more than three weeks
without a speaker,

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.968
Republicans got on the same page

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:24.901
and elected Mike Johnson
as the new Speaker of the House.

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:26.901
Yep, they found someone
just in time.

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:28.834
If the job stayed
open any longer,

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:31.234
it would have automatically
gone to Ryan Seacrest.

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:34.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.501
That's right,
Republicans said Mike Johnson

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.133
is their first choice

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:40.367
after the first 10 choices lost.

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:41.968
Then he -- Then him.

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:43.734
Let's just say
if speaker nominees

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:47.467
were "Star Wars" characters,
he's their Jar Jar.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:50.133
Let's just say if speaker
nominees were Halloween candy,

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:52.834
this guy is a Necco Wafer, okay?

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:55.267
It's like being at a restaurant
and hearing, "Do you have Coke?"

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:57.868
"No." "Pepsi?" "No."
"Sprite?" "No."

00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:00.267
"Fine, I guess I'll have
the Mike Johnson."

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:02.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:05.767
That's --

00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:07.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:13.334
That's right, the new Speaker
of the House is Mike Johnson.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:14.968
And if that name
sounds familiar,

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:18.601
it's 'cause it's
on every fake ID.

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:21.534
"Hi. I'm Mike Johnson.

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:25.534
Just two four-packs
of Mike's Hard Lemonade."

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:28.434
I read that Johnson is the most
inexperienced House Speaker

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:29.901
in modern history,

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:32.367
and a lot of people said
that his résumé is lacking.

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:34.801
Then George Santos was like,
"I can help you edit that.

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:37.567
I'm good at -- Just say that
you were president, yeah.

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:39.400
Just say you were
the president for four years.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.334
Who cares?"

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.667
Johnson is pretty controversial
because he led the effort

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:47.000
to overturn the 2020
presidential election.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.834
So basically,
whether or not he won today,

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:50.968
he was going to say he did.

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:52.601
Some more big news today.

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:56.067
The judge in former president
Trump's civil fraud trial

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:58.067
fined Trump $10,000

00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:01.133
for violating his gag order
a second time

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:03.701
and warned him not to do
it again or it'll be worse.

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.434
-Ooh.
-Yep.

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:07.701
Trump could be sentenced
to jail.

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:11.667
Or even worse, a brunch
with Eric and Don Jr.

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:13.267
[ As Trump ]
Send me to the clink.

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:15.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.601
[ Normal voice ]
Meanwhile, during Trump's day
in court yesterday,

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:19.200
one of his lawyers
claimed that at one point

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.367
Trump could have bought
multiple NFL teams.

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.234
Of course, Trump agrees,

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:26.300
and to show that he's
a big fan of the league,

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.767
he even defined
some common NFL terms.

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:30.133
-Oh.
-Yeah, let's see how he did.

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:32.501
First up, for hut, Trump said...

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:38.834
[ As Trump ]
Nobody beats it.

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:41.200
[ Normal voice ]
Next up, for handoff, he said...

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:45.734
Two words.
-Two words.

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:48.000
-Two words.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.534
Up next, for yard lines,
he said...

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:54.300
Wait, what is that?
What are you talking about?

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.133
I don't know what he's --
Why would he -- Why would he --

00:02:56.133 --> 00:02:57.634
He said it.
I don't know why he said it.

00:02:57.634 --> 00:02:59.033
-You're just reading
what he said.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:01.734
-Next up, for scramble,
he said...

00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:06.567
[ As Trump ] I don't like --
I don't want to play Scramble.

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:08.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:11.334
[ Normal voice ] Then for
the name Mahomes, he said...

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:14.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.601 --> 00:03:15.601
Come on, that's a good --

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:17.734
That's worth it right there.

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:20.033
That's worth
the price of admission.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.501
-Cute.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.801
Shout-out to the gals at work.
That was a cute one.

00:03:23.801 --> 00:03:25.267
-That was a good one there,
yeah.

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:26.300
There's more, though.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.400
Next up, for stiff arm,
he said...

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:32.100
Do we have a photo?
Oh, interesting. That's --

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.334 --> 00:03:36.767
-Ohhh!

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:39.334
-Then there's -- for 49ers,
he said...

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:44.400
-What?

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.267
-I don't know why -- Why would
he say all these things?

00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:48.100
-Why would he say that aloud?

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:50.501
Why would he write it down?

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:52.434
-And finally, for Steelers,
he said...

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.834
There you go. That's --
There you go.

00:03:56.834 --> 00:04:00.067
He knows the NFL.
He knows football.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.734
Well, switching gears,
in transportation news,

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:07.834
the FAA just got a new leader

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:10.801
after a year and a half
without anyone in charge.

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:12.467
Yeah, I guess for
the last year and a half,

00:04:12.467 --> 00:04:14.868
it's been every plane
for themselves.

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:16.501
Yeah, a year and a half.
Yeah.

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:19.300
Apparently he was
in boarding group D, so...

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:25.234
Some business news -- The
long-awaited Tesla Cybertruck

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:26.934
is set to become available
next month.

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:29.834
It's going to weigh
at least 8,000 pounds.

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:31.000
I'm not making that --
Here it is.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.334
You see the photo?

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:34.868
It weighs at least 8,000 pounds.

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:37.200
Yeah, and that's
before the holidays.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.267
Yeah, yeah, it's going to be
a gigantic truck.

00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:42.467
And every single one
will have this license plate.

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.701
I think that's interesting.
That's --

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:47.667
Why would -- Why would you --
Again, you don't have to.

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:48.734
-Wow.

00:04:48.734 --> 00:04:50.133
-They don't have to do that.

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:52.934
[ Applause ]

00:04:52.934 --> 00:04:54.133
Well, some TV news.

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:57.501
Today Netflix released
a new documentary series

00:04:57.501 --> 00:04:59.267
called "Life on Our Planet

00:04:59.267 --> 00:05:01.434
that's narrated
by Morgan Freeman.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.868
Yeah. We love --
Yeah, it's pretty cool.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.434
And it's actually
not the only show

00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:06.767
that Morgan Freeman
is narrating right now.

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:08.267
Take a look at this thing I saw.

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:11.734
-Welcome back
to "The Golden Bachelor."

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:16.934
Watch as the septuagenarian male
pursues multiple mates at once.

00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:18.601
He pauses for a long time

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:21.300
because he cannot
remember their names.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.901
Finally, he just throws out
a random name as a guess.

00:05:24.901 --> 00:05:25.901
-Ellen.

00:05:25.901 --> 00:05:28.033
-Whew, that was close.

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:30.000
Now it's off
to the Fantasy Suite,

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.300
which is Gerry's mating nest,

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:37.667
and his actions require the
assistance of a small blue pill.

00:05:37.667 --> 00:05:40.567
-No, it's interesting.
He does a great job.

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:42.467
Beautiful.

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:45.367
[ Applause ]

00:05:45.367 --> 00:05:46.934
Well, this is going viral.

00:05:46.934 --> 00:05:50.067
At a Taco Bell in Indiana,
an employee was caught

00:05:50.067 --> 00:05:55.400
giving one of their co-workers
a haircut in the kitchen.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.400
The only thing worse
than finding one long hair

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:00.200
in your food is finding
500 short ones, don't you think?

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.934
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.934 --> 00:06:04.801
I actually prefer
to spend a few extra bucks

00:06:04.801 --> 00:06:06.434
and get my hair cut at Chipotle.

00:06:06.434 --> 00:06:07.934
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.767
Meanwhile, at a McDonald's
in the U.K.,

00:06:10.767 --> 00:06:12.801
one mom said that she found
a cigarette butt

00:06:12.801 --> 00:06:15.400
in her son's Happy Meal.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:16.834
Even worse, the manager said,

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:19.300
"Sorry, I only smoke
when I'm getting a haircut."

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.934
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.934 --> 00:06:22.701
A cigarette butt
in a Happy Meal.

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:25.501
Meanwhile, in a Burger King
kid's meal, that's the toy.

00:06:25.501 --> 00:06:28.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:31.033
Play with it all you want.
Come back, get --

00:06:31.033 --> 00:06:35.133
Collect all the
cigarette butts you want.

00:06:35.133 --> 00:06:36.868
Finally, have you guys
ever noticed

00:06:36.868 --> 00:06:39.033
when you start typing
something on Google,

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:42.400
it automatically tries to
complete the search for you?

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.000
Yeah, it autofills
what you're looking for,

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.000
but sometimes their suggestions
are a little off, I think.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.033
I'll show you what I mean.

00:06:47.033 --> 00:06:48.634
It's time for
"Google Autofails."

00:06:48.634 --> 00:06:49.834
Here we go.

00:06:49.834 --> 00:06:54.133
-♪ Google Autofails, yeah ♪

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:57.934
-Look at what I typed in today.
Today I typed in...

00:07:00.801 --> 00:07:02.501
And these three things
popped up...

00:07:07.167 --> 00:07:09.100
I go, no -- no one wants that.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:11.934
I don't want to see that.

00:07:11.934 --> 00:07:13.901
Here's another one I typed in.
I typed in...

00:07:16.033 --> 00:07:17.367
And it said...

00:07:24.534 --> 00:07:26.834
I go, that's probably why.

00:07:26.834 --> 00:07:28.467
But that's not
what I was typing.

00:07:28.467 --> 00:07:31.267
[ Applause ]

00:07:31.267 --> 00:07:32.400
After that, I typed in...

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.400
It said...

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.234
[ Applause ]

00:07:43.234 --> 00:07:44.501
Disaster.

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.067
Next up, I typed in...

00:07:51.734 --> 00:07:53.133
And it autofilled...

00:07:57.767 --> 00:07:59.501
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:07:59.501 --> 00:08:01.067
♪ Hey, there, Delilah ♪

00:08:01.067 --> 00:08:03.801
♪ There is something
I will tell you ♪

00:08:05.868 --> 00:08:07.033
After that, I typed in...

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.300
And it said...

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.501
[ Applause ]

00:08:15.501 --> 00:08:18.100
[ As Elvis ] Well, you ain't
seen this side of the story yet.

00:08:20.901 --> 00:08:23.501
You ain't seen this side
of me yet, man. Come on.

00:08:23.501 --> 00:08:25.000
-Hyah!

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.234
-[ Normal voice ]
Next up, I typed in...

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.467
And it said...

00:08:33.634 --> 00:08:35.000
[ Laughter ]

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.734
[ Applause ]

00:08:36.734 --> 00:08:39.000
Whee!

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.467
-So cute.

00:08:40.467 --> 00:08:41.801
-Here's another one.
I typed in...

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.000
It said...

00:08:48.901 --> 00:08:51.100
[ Applause ]

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:52.501
And you traded him?

00:08:52.501 --> 00:08:54.267
-Wow.
-You traded him?

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:56.033
Oh, my God, that's terrible.

00:08:56.033 --> 00:08:57.901
And you traded him?
You did?

00:08:57.901 --> 00:08:59.701
Oh, I can't believe it.
-Wow.

00:08:59.701 --> 00:09:02.033
-And he wouldn't trade you back?

00:09:02.033 --> 00:09:03.634
Oh, man.

00:09:03.634 --> 00:09:04.968
-Wow.
-Wow.

00:09:04.968 --> 00:09:06.667
And he didn't play?

00:09:06.667 --> 00:09:08.767
Oh, wow.

00:09:08.767 --> 00:09:11.000
-He got injured?
-In the game?

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:13.100
-Oh, man.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:15.901
Oh, I got to go back
to my files.

00:09:15.901 --> 00:09:16.934
[ Laughter ]

00:09:16.934 --> 00:09:18.067
-What files do you
have to get to?

00:09:18.067 --> 00:09:20.000
-Yeah, just a bunch of files.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.300
-Wait, you're telling me
he's not playing?

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:23.701
He's sick this week?

00:09:23.701 --> 00:09:26.167
-Wow.
-Man. That's terrible.

00:09:26.167 --> 00:09:28.400
[ Laughs ]

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:29.501
Finally, I typed in...

00:09:30.634 --> 00:09:31.667
And it said...

00:09:35.901 --> 00:09:37.434
Stick around, everybody.

00:09:37.434 --> 00:09:38.834
When we come back,
we're doing something

00:09:38.834 --> 00:09:41.634
fun and scary with Cameron Diaz.

